    "summary": "Soaring Dark Star, monster Playin', tight China>Rider flow",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering Dark Star → Truckin' → Morning Dew sequence and an inspired Playin' in the Band. China Cat Sunflower into I Know You Rider opens the night with crisp interplay, while Bird Song and Wave That Flag keep the energy high throughout.",
    "review": "March 16, 1973 at Nassau Coliseum captured one of the spring ’73 peaks. From the opening China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider sandwich to a relentless second set, the band is locked in – Jerry’s tone is immaculate and his solos on Dark Star and Playin' are downright electrifying. Phil’s “smoking” bass underpins every jam, while Keith adds lush piano textures that lift the transitions. Bill Kreutzmann drives the grooves with deep‑zen precision, especially during the monster Dark Star → Truckin' → Morning Dew stretch. Highlights like Bird Song, Wave That Flag, and a seamless Promised Land > Bertha > Greatest Story flow keep the momentum soaring, making this concert a must‑listen for any Deadhead.",
